   3.987992549874106*^9, 3.987992550206791*^9}, {3.991485257815167*^9, 
   3.991485258276855*^9}, {3.998578886308236*^9, 3.9985788926423545`*^9}, {
   3.9985838326585884`*^9, 
   3.998583833623723*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f1e6e928-a243-4262-8b22-\
e4fb77587ccb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["1. The output data are organized as {number of pairs k, {all \
eigenvalues}} in GnPairing.\n2. The reference  output data are organized as \
{k, t[s], the number of eigenvalues, {the first a few eigenvalues}}, where \
t[s] is the CPU time in seconds. \n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 1.]],
 StyleBox["3. In the  reference  output for p>=3, only  results with  k less \
than the maximum number of  pairs are shown. In this case,  the number of \
eigenvalues may be less than the actual value when the maximum number of  \
pairs are large, due to  insufficient accuracy in finding the root of the \
polynomial in the algorithm of Ref. [34] .  This is also the reason to \
construct the GnPairing code.\n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1., 0., 0.]],
 StyleBox["4. These tests clearly shown that  the Gnpairing code is valid.",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 1., 0.]],
 StyleBox["\n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1., 0., 0.]]
}], "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.875969869810183*^9, 3.87596990407795*^9}, {
   3.99857893448894*^9, 3.998578993627877*^9}, {3.998579028217416*^9, 
   3.9985792676662693`*^9}, {3.998579315763386*^9, 3.998579387435539*^9}, {
